# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# un-claude — .gitignore
#
# Anything matching a line in this file is invisible to git. It is never
# committed and never pushed to GitHub. Everything else in this folder will be
# committed once staged.
#
# Read this file before adding to it. The first block is load-bearing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- SECRETS. Nothing in this block may ever reach GitHub. -----------------

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. This is the file that holds the Moonshot
# API key and points this project at Kimi. It is the single most important
# line in this file. If this line is ever deleted, the next commit publishes
# the key to GitHub.
#
# Consequence, recorded here on purpose: because this file is ignored, the
# Kimi configuration does not travel with the repository. A fresh clone of
# un-claude on another machine runs on Claude, not Kimi, until this file is
# recreated by hand. That is the correct trade — a key must not leak — but it
# is a trap if nobody wrote it down. It is written down.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Environment files in every common form. Real values live in these; only the
# committed .env.example template carries variable names with empty values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Keys, certificates and credential files, matched by extension. Deliberately
# broad. A false positive here costs nothing; a false negative leaks a secret.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
credentials.json


# --- macOS clutter ----------------------------------------------------------

# Finder writes these into every folder it displays. They are noise and they
# are never wanted in a commit.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store


# --- Dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------

# The tech stack for this project is not chosen yet. These entries cover the
# common cases in advance, so that a stray install command cannot dump tens of
# thousands of machine-generated files into a commit. Stack-specific entries
# get added when the stack is decided.
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/


# --- Editor and machine-local state -----------------------------------------

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo


# --- Scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Working files that are not part of the durable record. If something in here
# turns out to matter, it should be moved into the docs tree, not un-ignored.
scratch/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 18 Aug 2026 when MakerKit Lite was merged in. Build artefacts and
# dependency folders only. The secret rules above are ours and take priority.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.js
coverage
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
build
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.env*.local
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed
.contentlayer/
.prds/
.env*

# Engine: local Python packages and caches, never committed
engine/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# apps/web/.env holds the kit's non-secret configuration: product name, title,
# theme, which auth methods are on. Every value is NEXT_PUBLIC_ and therefore
# ships to browsers anyway. Vercel's `vercel link` added the .env* rule above,
# which silently blocked this file and made every deployment fail for hours
# while the old build kept serving. See docs/07-runbook.md.
!apps/web/.env
